        <span class="compare-label">Before</span>
        <p>“Did a summer internship at a small company.”</p>
      </div>
      <div class="compare-block good">
        <span class="compare-label">After — ATS-aligned</span>
        <p>“Supported digital marketing operations during a 6-week internship, including social media content planning and basic performance analytics.”</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ MISTAKES ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:24px;">Common mistakes on internship resumes</h2>
    <div class="mistakes">
      
      <div class="mistake"><div><strong>Not stating availability</strong><p>Forces the recruiter to guess your duration and timing.</p></div></div>
      
      <div class="mistake"><div><strong>Reusing a full-time-job resume as-is</strong><p>Internship expectations differ — education and coursework should lead.</p></div></div>
      
      <div class="mistake"><div><strong>Omitting short or unpaid work</strong><p>A belief it “doesn't count” leaves out legitimate content.</p></div></div>
      
      <div class="mistake"><div><strong>Overloading with unrelated coursework</strong><p>List only subjects relevant to the internship's function.</p></div></div>
      
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ ATS CONSIDERATIONS ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:20px;">ATS considerations</h2>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Keep availability/duration in plain text near the top, not buried in a paragraph — some parsers extract only structured fields well.</li><li>Standard section headings remain the safest choice for internship portals that often run their own ATS layer.</li><li>Avoid embedding availability or contact details inside a header/footer — this content is sometimes not extracted.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ CHECKLIST ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:22px;">Quick checklist before you apply</h2>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Availability and duration clearly stated</li><li>Education section leads the resume</li><li>At least 2 relevant projects listed with outcomes</li><li>Any prior internship or part-time work included, however short</li><li>Resume kept to one page</li><li>Contact details in the body text, not header/footer only</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

