<!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:8px;">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom:10px;">Straight answers to what people usually ask before applying.</p>
    <div>
      
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Do I need prior internship experience to apply for an internship? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>No — most applicants at this stage have limited or no prior internship experience; projects and coursework are valid substitutes.</p></div>
      </details>
      
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Should I state my availability on the resume? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes — stating your available duration and start date near the top helps recruiters quickly assess fit for time-bound roles.</p></div>
      </details>
      
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How long should an internship resume be? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>One page is standard for internship applications.</p></div>
      </details>
      
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Can I include college club or event coordination roles? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, if relevant to the internship's function — describe your specific contribution and outcome.</p></div>
      </details>
      
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Should my internship resume look different from a job resume? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes — it typically emphasizes education, coursework, and availability more heavily.</p></div>
      </details>
      
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">What if I've only done one very short internship? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Include it and describe the specific tasks and outcomes, even briefly — it's still relevant experience.</p></div>
      </details>
      
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

